      "title": "Pollutant falls as gas rises through the packing",
      "description": "Acid gases (e.g. H₂S, HCl, SO₂, Cl₂) are absorbed into the liquor and neutralised by caustic (e.g. H₂S + 2 NaOH → Na₂S + 2 H₂O). Counter-current flow keeps the strongest liquor meeting the cleanest gas, so removal can exceed 99 %. Design uses liquid-to-gas ratio, packing height (NTU × HTU) and pH control; spent liquor is bled off and fresh caustic added.",
